{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-pf.6.1:000061:note_appended:bob-cli-pf.6.1.4:989ebdc635a845482f6ec639d1b8f1fa8a68318cb1c7547df11032a4803de389","timestamp":"2026-11-24T11:51:35Z","actor":"bob-cli-pf.6.1.4--1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-pf.6.1.4","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Monitor g5645dfc9na3 proved protected-note bytes unchanged with no write transitions; remaining NO-GO was custom-shortcut-add-owned and sidebar-native. Isolated real Obsidian 1.15.1 diagnosis: closeEditor sent only one Escape from Add mode, leaving a browse modal whose scope intercepted the next shortcut. Cleanup now follows the existing menu/stage/filter/modal Escape ladder, observes dismissal, and fails if any modal persists. Sidebar probe used unregistered file-properties:open and matched All Properties; now invokes observed properties:open-local, targets only file-properties, reveals/loads its leaf, and requires visible usable native controls. Focused real-app checks for Mod+;, command dispatch, Alt+P, bank/ordinary native state and sidebar all pass on the unchanged production bundle. Fixed host test mocks to retain both adapter and shared coordinator listeners. 34 focused unit tests and build:check pass. Full matrix plus screenshot inspection still required; a monitored rerun also collects clean-HEAD controls for tracked n0 held-lock and km timing failures. No memory or production source changes."}}
